IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mvwaci-ciss`
IMPORT `mvwaci-qa`

-- Motor Vehicle and Workplace Accidents (Catastrophic Injuries) Act 2016 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (mvwaci-qa.l4):
-- every exported question, for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for each role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the answer
-- must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation ("it is an assumed term").
-- Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value under which the situation does
-- not hold, every later input ASSUMEd. Where a question takes the answer of an earlier one (whether the Act applies as a
-- motor vehicle injury, how the Act takes the injury, whether s 18 covers an expense), the comparison with the baseline
-- export gives it the answer the baseline gives on the same records. Where the situation says no motor vehicle was involved, or that the person was not
-- injured as a worker, the facts of that kind are ASSUMEd too, which shows the form need not ask them. For the injured
-- person (the baseline's seat), cases check that the answer equals the baseline export's on the same facts, built here as
-- the baseline's own records. Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text; whether an injury meets the
-- prescribed criteria is a stated fact, since no regulations are deposited.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives: Chloe's licensed car (c074), alone on a WA road, or a passenger while Liam drives negligently.
-- The workplace, carer and provider cases are illustrative.
--
-- Written by the scratchpad script gen_mv_cases.py, which only spells out the argument lists.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked way` IS A `How it happened`
ASSUME `an unasked injury` IS A `How I was injured`
ASSUME `an unasked place` IS A `My place in the scheme`
ASSUME `an unasked place of theirs` IS A `Their place in the scheme`
ASSUME `an unasked kind of need` IS A `The kind of need`
ASSUME `an unasked decision` IS A `The decision`
ASSUME `an unasked way the Act takes it` IS A `How the Act takes my injury`
ASSUME `an unasked time` IS A `When the care need arises`
ASSUME `an unasked time of care` IS A `When I give the care`
ASSUME `an unasked kind of service` IS A `Kind of service`
ASSUME `an unasked kind` IS A `What kind of need it is`
ASSUME `an unasked participation of theirs` IS A `Their participation when I gave the care`

`as the injured person` MEANS `I was injured in a motor vehicle accident or at work`
`as the carer` MEANS `I act for, or care for, someone who was injured`
`as the provider` MEANS `I provide treatment, care or support to people in the scheme`

`a motor vehicle, not as a worker` MEANS `in an incident involving a motor vehicle, and not as a worker`
`as a worker, no motor vehicle` MEANS `as a worker, in an incident not involving a motor vehicle`
`as a worker, with a motor vehicle` MEANS `as a worker, in an incident involving a motor vehicle`

`not accepted` MEANS `I have not been accepted into the scheme`
`interim participant` MEANS `I am an interim participant`
`lifetime participant` MEANS `I am a lifetime participant`
`former interim participant` MEANS `my interim participation has ended, and I was not made a lifetime participant`
`former lifetime participant, notified` MEANS `I was a lifetime participant until notified that I am no longer eligible`

-- The baseline's own records, for the cases that compare with the baseline export.
`the runaway car` MEANS `The accident` WITH
    `how it happened` IS `a motor vehicle running out of control`
    `it happened in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `it happened on or after 1 July 2016` IS TRUE
    `an owner or driver is liable in negligence for my injury` IS FALSE
    `it happened on private land` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved had WA compulsory third party insurance` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved was licensed interstate and under that place's compulsory scheme` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved was in a motor sports event` IS FALSE
    `it resulted from a terrorist act` IS FALSE

`the worker struck by a negligent driver` MEANS `The accident` WITH
    `how it happened` IS `a collision, or action to avoid one, with a motor vehicle, moving or stationary`
    `it happened in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `it happened on or after 1 July 2016` IS TRUE
    `an owner or driver is liable in negligence for my injury` IS TRUE
    `it happened on private land` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved had WA compulsory third party insurance` IS TRUE
    `a vehicle involved was licensed interstate and under that place's compulsory scheme` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved was in a motor sports event` IS FALSE
    `it resulted from a terrorist act` IS FALSE

`Chloe alone on a WA road` MEANS `The accident` WITH
    `how it happened` IS `the driving of a motor vehicle`
    `it happened in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `it happened on or after 1 July 2016` IS TRUE
    `an owner or driver is liable in negligence for my injury` IS FALSE
    `it happened on private land` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved had WA compulsory third party insurance` IS TRUE
    `a vehicle involved was licensed interstate and under that place's compulsory scheme` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved was in a motor sports event` IS FALSE
    `it resulted from a terrorist act` IS FALSE

`no accident of the Act's kind` MEANS `The accident` WITH
    `how it happened` IS `none of these`
    `it happened in Western Australia` IS FALSE
    `it happened on or after 1 July 2016` IS FALSE
    `an owner or driver is liable in negligence for my injury` IS FALSE
    `it happened on private land` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved had WA compulsory third party insurance` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved was licensed interstate and under that place's compulsory scheme` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved was in a motor sports event` IS FALSE
    `it resulted from a terrorist act` IS FALSE

`an interstate car on a farm` MEANS `The accident` WITH
    `how it happened` IS `a collision, or action to avoid one, with a motor vehicle, moving or stationary`
    `it happened in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `it happened on or after 1 July 2016` IS TRUE
    `an owner or driver is liable in negligence for my injury` IS FALSE
    `it happened on private land` IS TRUE
    `a vehicle involved had WA compulsory third party insurance` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved was licensed interstate and under that place's compulsory scheme` IS TRUE
    `a vehicle involved was in a motor sports event` IS FALSE
    `it resulted from a terrorist act` IS FALSE

`a car used in a terrorist act` MEANS `The accident` WITH
    `how it happened` IS `the driving of a motor vehicle`
    `it happened in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `it happened on or after 1 July 2016` IS TRUE
    `an owner or driver is liable in negligence for my injury` IS FALSE
    `it happened on private land` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved had WA compulsory third party insurance` IS TRUE
    `a vehicle involved was licensed interstate and under that place's compulsory scheme` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved was in a motor sports event` IS FALSE
    `it resulted from a terrorist act` IS TRUE

`not a work injury` MEANS `The work injury` WITH
    `I am a worker under the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023` IS FALSE
    `workers' compensation is payable for my injury` IS FALSE
    `it happened on or after 1 July 2024` IS FALSE
    `I have claimed workers' compensation for it` IS FALSE
    `liability was accepted, taken to be accepted, or decided by an arbitrator` IS FALSE

`the struck worker's case` MEANS `My case` WITH
    `the accident` IS `the worker struck by a negligent driver`
    `the work injury` IS `a work injury with liability accepted`
    `my injury meets the prescribed criteria for a catastrophic injury` IS TRUE
    `I meet the prescribed criteria for lifetime participation` IS FALSE
    `I have been awarded damages for my future care by final judgment or binding settlement` IS FALSE
    `I reside in Australia` IS TRUE

`a warehouse worker's case` MEANS `My case` WITH
    `the accident` IS `no accident of the Act's kind`
    `the work injury` IS `a work injury with liability accepted`
    `my injury meets the prescribed criteria for a catastrophic injury` IS TRUE
    `I meet the prescribed criteria for lifetime participation` IS FALSE
    `I have been awarded damages for my future care by final judgment or binding settlement` IS FALSE
    `I reside in Australia` IS FALSE

`Chloe's case` MEANS `My case` WITH
    `the accident` IS `Chloe alone on a WA road`
    `the work injury` IS `not a work injury`
    `my injury meets the prescribed criteria for a catastrophic injury` IS TRUE
    `I meet the prescribed criteria for lifetime participation` IS TRUE
    `I have been awarded damages for my future care by final judgment or binding settlement` IS FALSE
    `I reside in Australia` IS FALSE

`assessed attendant care, given free, the Commission electing` MEANS `The expense` WITH
    `the kind of need` IS `attendant care services`
    `it is of a kind the regulations exclude` IS FALSE
    `the Commission assessed it as a necessary and reasonable need related to my injury` IS TRUE
    `the expense is necessary and reasonable` IS TRUE
    `I was a participant when it was incurred` IS TRUE
    `my participation was suspended at the time` IS FALSE
    `it was given to me free` IS TRUE
    `it was given while I was outside Australia` IS FALSE
    `I am a child and it is an ordinary cost of raising a child` IS FALSE
    `it had to come from a registered provider and did not` IS FALSE
    `it was provided in breach of the regulations` IS FALSE
    `the regulations exclude it from payment` IS FALSE
    `the Commission elects to pay it anyway` IS TRUE

`assessed rehabilitation abroad` MEANS `The expense` WITH
    `the kind of need` IS `rehabilitation`
    `it is of a kind the regulations exclude` IS FALSE
    `the Commission assessed it as a necessary and reasonable need related to my injury` IS TRUE
    `the expense is necessary and reasonable` IS TRUE
    `I was a participant when it was incurred` IS TRUE
    `my participation was suspended at the time` IS FALSE
    `it was given to me free` IS FALSE
    `it was given while I was outside Australia` IS TRUE
    `I am a child and it is an ordinary cost of raising a child` IS FALSE
    `it had to come from a registered provider and did not` IS FALSE
    `it was provided in breach of the regulations` IS FALSE
    `the regulations exclude it from payment` IS FALSE
    `the Commission elects to pay it anyway` IS FALSE

§§ `The injured person`

§§§ `ss 4, 5, 5A`

-- s 4(2)(a)
#ASSERT `Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident under the Act` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `the driving of a motor vehicle` EQUALS yes
-- falling from a parked truck: none of s 4(2)
#ASSERT `Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident under the Act` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `none of these` EQUALS no
-- s 4(3), the baseline's answer
#ASSERT `Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident under the Act` `as the injured person` `as a worker, with a motor vehicle` `helping at the scene of a motor vehicle accident` EQUALS `yes if` (`Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident` `helping at the scene of a motor vehicle accident`)
#ASSERT `Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident under the Act` `as the injured person` `as a worker, no motor vehicle` `an unasked way` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident under the Act` `as the carer` `an unasked injury` `an unasked way` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident under the Act` `as the provider` `an unasked injury` `an unasked way` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
-- c074, Chloe alone on a WA road: inside the scheme
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `the driving of a motor vehicle` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
-- c074, Chloe a passenger, Liam negligent: s 5(3)
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `the driving of a motor vehicle` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
-- private land, no CTP: s 5(4)
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `a collision, or action to avoid one, with a motor vehicle, moving or stationary` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
-- an uninsured car out of control on a road, no one negligent: s 5(4) does not reach roads
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `a motor vehicle running out of control` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
-- the baseline's answer on the same facts
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `a motor vehicle running out of control` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does the Act apply to my motor vehicle injury` `the runaway car`)
-- s 5(4)(b): the interstate cover, asked with the WA cover as one fact
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `a collision, or action to avoid one, with a motor vehicle, moving or stationary` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does the Act apply to my motor vehicle injury` `an interstate car on a farm`)
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `a collision, or action to avoid one, with a motor vehicle, moving or stationary` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
-- s 5(5)(b): a terrorist act, asked with a motor sports event as one fact
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `the driving of a motor vehicle` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does the Act apply to my motor vehicle injury` `a car used in a terrorist act`)
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` `the driving of a motor vehicle` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the injured person` `as a worker, no motor vehicle` `an unasked way` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the carer` `an unasked injury` `an unasked way` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury in a motor vehicle accident` `as the provider` `an unasked injury` `an unasked way` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
-- a warehouse worker, claim accepted: s 5A(2), (3); nothing about a vehicle is asked
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury as a workplace injury` `as the injured person` `as a worker, no motor vehicle` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `an unasked fact` EQUALS yes
-- claim not yet accepted: no established entitlement, s 5A(3)
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury as a workplace injury` `as the injured person` `as a worker, no motor vehicle` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `an unasked fact` EQUALS no
-- a worker struck by a negligent driver: s 5(3) takes it out as a motor vehicle injury, so s 5A(4) does not divert it (finding 6)
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury as a workplace injury` `as the injured person` `as a worker, with a motor vehicle` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
