#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my injury as a workplace injury` `as the provider` `an unasked injury` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
-- nothing about work is asked of someone not injured as a worker
#ASSERT `Does the Act take my injury as a motor vehicle injury, a workplace injury, or not at all` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` TRUE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `the Act takes my injury` `as a motor vehicle injury`
-- nothing about a vehicle is asked of someone injured without one
#ASSERT `Does the Act take my injury as a motor vehicle injury, a workplace injury, or not at all` `as the injured person` `as a worker, no motor vehicle` `an unasked fact` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Act takes my injury` `as a workplace injury`
#ASSERT `Does the Act take my injury as a motor vehicle injury, a workplace injury, or not at all` `as the injured person` `as a worker, with a motor vehicle` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Act takes my injury` `as a motor vehicle injury`
#ASSERT `Does the Act take my injury as a motor vehicle injury, a workplace injury, or not at all` `as the injured person` `as a worker, with a motor vehicle` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Act takes my injury` `as a workplace injury`
#ASSERT `Does the Act take my injury as a motor vehicle injury, a workplace injury, or not at all` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` FALSE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `the Act takes my injury` `not at all`
-- the baseline's answer on the same facts
#ASSERT `Does the Act take my injury as a motor vehicle injury, a workplace injury, or not at all` `as the injured person` `as a worker, with a motor vehicle` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Act takes my injury` (`How does the Act take my injury` `the worker struck by a negligent driver` `a work injury with liability accepted`)
#ASSERT `Does the Act take my injury as a motor vehicle injury, a workplace injury, or not at all` `as the injured person` `a motor vehicle, not as a worker` TRUE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `the Act takes my injury` (`How does the Act take my injury` `Chloe alone on a WA road` `not a work injury`)
#ASSERT `Does the Act take my injury as a motor vehicle injury, a workplace injury, or not at all` `as the carer` `an unasked injury` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does the Act take my injury as a motor vehicle injury, a workplace injury, or not at all` `as the provider` `an unasked injury` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 3, 8, 9, 34(2)(a)`

-- c074, Chloe alone, the criteria met
